{"question_text": {"স্পেশাল বিসিএস (স্বাস্থ্য) - লং কোর্স": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Important poisoning substance in South Asia?", "option1": "Amphetamine", "option2": "Alcohol ", "option3": "Paraquat", "option4": "Paracetamol ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2464.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1036\" height=\"974\" />"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Substance causing high lactate acidosis?", "option1": "Metformin", "option2": "Salicylates", "option3": "Methanol", "option4": "Ethylene glycol", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2465.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Use of activated charcoal is ineffective in case of which substance?", "option1": "Phenobarbital", "option2": "Theophylline", "option3": "Lithium", "option4": "Quinine", "answer": "3", "exp": "Multiple doses of activated charcoal is effective against other substances.<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2466.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1006\" height=\"535\" />"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Which is the antidote used in Isoniazid poisoning?", "option1": "Methionine ", "option2": "Pyridoxine", "option3": "Glucarpidase", "option4": "Sodium thiosulphate", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2467.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Major toxic effect of metformin is-", "option1": "Lactic acidosis ", "option2": "Abdominal pain ", "option3": "Hypoglycaemia ", "option4": "Myopathy ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<strong>Davidson Page 228<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2468.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"959\" height=\"1035\" /></strong>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Example of stimulant substance-", "option1": "Heroin", "option2": "Fentanyl", "option3": "Pethidine", "option4": "Ephedrine", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2469.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1010\" height=\"678\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Clinical feature of Lead poisoning?", "option1": "Cyanosis", "option2": "Nephrotoxicity ", "option3": "Profound hypokalaemia ", "option4": "Perioral paraesthesia", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2472.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1034\" height=\"988\" />"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Early feature of carbon monoxide poisoning-", "option1": "Ataxia", "option2": "Tachypnoea", "option3": "Nystagmus ", "option4": "Drowsiness ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<strong>Davidson Page 231<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2474.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></strong>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Which poison is effectively eliminated by haemodialysis?", "option1": "Phenytoin ", "option2": "Lithium", "option3": "Carbamazepine", "option4": "Theophylline", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2475.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1070\" height=\"732\" />"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which is an example of choking agents?", "option1": "Nitrogen", "option2": "Chlorine", "option3": "Novichok agents", "option4": "Cyanide ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2470.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) T cells are originated from-", "option1": "Cortex", "option2": "Paracortex", "option3": "Medulla", "option4": "Germinal centre", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2476.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"885\" height=\"722\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Function of IL-8-", "option1": "Activate vascular endothelium", "option2": "Stimulate the acute phase response", "option3": "Stimulate monocyte chemotaxis", "option4": "Stimulate neutrophil maturation and chemotaxis", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2477.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Which of the following cytokines shows antiviral activity?", "option1": "Interferon-alpha (IFN-α)", "option2": "Interferon-gamma (IFN-γ)", "option3": "Tumour necrosis factor alpha (TNF-α)", "option4": "Interleukin-1 (IL-1)", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2478.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Which immunoglobulin is responsible for mucosal defence?", "option1": "IgG", "option2": "IgA", "option3": "IgM", "option4": "IgE", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2479.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1030\" height=\"543\" />"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Example of type III hypersensitivity-", "option1": "Hashimoto’s thyroiditis", "option2": "Goodpasture's disease", "option3": "Systemic lupus erythematosus", "option4": "Autoimmune haemolytic anaemia", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2481.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"906\" height=\"1286\" />"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Condition associated with type II cryoglobulins-", "option1": "Waldenström macroglobulinaemia", "option2": "Hepatitis B", "option3": "Hepatitis C ", "option4": "systemic lupus erythematosus", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2482.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Hereditary angioedema occurs due to-", "option1": "IgE-mediated degradation of mast cells", "option2": "C1 inhibitor deficiency", "option3": "Non-IgE-mediated degranulation of mast cells", "option4": "Inhibition of breakdown of bradykinin", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2483.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Which of the following conditions is a major adverse effect of Ciclosporin?", "option1": "Nephrotoxicity", "option2": "Hepatotoxicity", "option3": "Gingival hypertrophy", "option4": "Leucopenia", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2484.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"841\" height=\"1445\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Failure of Thymic development leads to-", "option1": "Cytokine deficiencies", "option2": "Severe combined immune deficiency", "option3": "Specific antibody deficiency", "option4": "DiGeorge syndrome", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2487.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Component of adaptive immune system-", "option1": "Neutrophil ", "option2": "Natural killer cell", "option3": "Antigen presenting cell", "option4": "Mast cell", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2488.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Genotype of Down syndrome is-", "option1": "47,XXY", "option2": "47,XYY", "option3": "47,XY", "option4": "45,XO", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2499_KgrDfa6.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Example of autosomal dominant condition-", "option1": "Cystic fibrosis", "option2": "Haemochromatosis", "option3": "Hereditary spherocytosis", "option4": "Sickle cell disease", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2491.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) In autosomal recessive inheritance-", "option1": "Males and females are usually affected in roughly equal numbers", "option2": "There are affected individuals in each generation", "option3": "Parents are blood-related", "option4": "The gene can be transmitted from female carriers to their sons", "answer": "3", "exp": "<strong>Davidson Page : 46</strong><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2492.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Example of imprinting disorder-", "option1": "Gilbert syndrome", "option2": "Prader–Willi syndrome\r\n", "option3": "Alport syndrome\r\n", "option4": "Kartagener syndrome", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2493.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1070\" height=\"446\" />"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Gene responsible for MEN 2a syndrome-", "option1": "APC", "option2": "MEN1", "option3": "MEN2", "option4": "RET", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2494_RJpgPnS.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Ovarian carcinoma is associated with-", "option1": "BRCA2 gene", "option2": "TP53 gene", "option3": "RET gene", "option4": "RB1 gene", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2495.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Example of non coding repeat expansion disorder -", "option1": "Spinocerebellar ataxia ", "option2": "Friedreich’s ataxia", "option3": "Spinobulbar muscular atrophy", "option4": "Huntington’s disease", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2496.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1070\" height=\"803\" />"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Generation of a premature stop codon is called-", "option1": "Synonymous ", "option2": "Non synonymous ", "option3": "Nonsense variant", "option4": "Neutral variant", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2497.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"871\" height=\"1014\" />"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Synthesis of cellular components occur at which stage of cell division?", "option1": "G0", "option2": "G1", "option3": "G2", "option4": "S", "answer": "2", "exp": "<strong>Davidson Page : 40<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2498.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1009\" height=\"459\" /></strong>"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Numerical chromosomal abnormality is seen in-", "option1": "Prader–Willi syndrome", "option2": "Patau syndrome ", "option3": "Di George syndrome\r\n", "option4": "Angelman syndrome", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2499.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 6125, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "900000", "is_omr": false, "omr_time": "7200000", "examname": "Sep 17, 2024", "type": "BCS-Health-Long", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}